- Story & Context: When federal gendarmes finally poured quick-drying cement down the access stairs in 1991 to seal the complex permanently, local legend claimed the band's matriarch slipped past the perimeter carrying a battery-rigged combo organ on a stainless-steel equipment dolly. Squatters living near the ventilation grates insisted that during October freezes, her minor-key chaconne still circled the buried ring like an echo that refused to dissipate, accompanied by the dry tapping of dead hornets falling from the vents. When spelunkers cracked the drainage sluice months later, they found only spent magnesium flares, velvet ribbon, and a quarter-inch master tape scrawled with the haunting command, "follow the beam until your exoskeleton cracks."
